<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-DBS Bank 1H net profit up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-DBS Bank 1H net profit up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		  (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     358.29    vs    316.95</p>
<p>    Dividend  (cents)		9.0     vs	8.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	    103.00    vs     92.00</p>
<p>    Group interest income(bln)   1.35    vs	1.10</p>
<p>    Group interest expense     888.97    vs    682.43</p>
<p>    Group net interest income  462.85    vs    414.84</p>
<p>    Group fees and commissions 143.22    vs    123.73</p>
<p>    Group dividends		 62.10    vs     49.22</p>
<p>    Group rental		    16.15    vs     16.18</p>
<p>    Group other income	    57.42    vs     73.50</p>
<p>    Group pretax profit	  449.02    vs    403.57</p>
<p>    Group tax			 90.65    vs     86.23</p>
<p>    Parent net profit	    316.99    vs    268.61</p>
<p>    Parent interest income(bln)  1.24    vs	0.99</p>
<p>    Parent interest expense    836.52    vs    638.11</p>
<p>    Parent net interest income 404.35    vs    354.65</p>
<p>Last day books open: August 20, 1997</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: September 2, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Full name is The Development Bank of Singapore.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
